<title>HONDURAS: Honduras to concession four airports in 1998.</title>
<headline>Honduras to concession four airports in 1998.</headline>
<dateline>TEGUCIGALPA, Honduras 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honduras next year will grant a concession to a private firm to operate four airports around the country, Central Bank Vice-President Daniel Figueroa said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The concession will last 20 years and covers the airports of the capital Tegucigalpa, the second city of San Pedro Sula and the smaller airports of La Ceiba and Isla de Roatan in the eastern part of the country.</p>
<p>Figueroa said bidding will get underway soon and the concession will be awarded in March1998.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Palencia, Honduras bureau +504 32-78-98))</p>
